### The 3-Step Stream Reboot

When `cin` encounters data that does not match the target variable type, it sets an internal error flag.

![C++ Error Recovery Architecture](assets/l30-errors-anatomy.en.svg)

#### The Reboot Sequence

```cpp
int reading;
cin >> reading;

if (cin.fail()) {
    // 1. Reset error flags so the stream can work again
    cin.clear();

    // 2. Read and discard the offending bad token
    string junk;
    cin >> junk;

    // 3. Fall back to a safe default value
    reading = 50;
}
```

#### Range Sanitization
Even if input syntax is valid, sensor hardware may transmit sentinel error codes (like `-999` on disconnection) or physically impossible values (altitude `-50` or battery `150`).

Defensive code always validates boundaries:
```cpp
if (reading < 0 || reading > 100) {
    reading = 50; // Substitute emergency fallback
}
```
